@startuml
title Class Diagram - Canopée (Real-Time Messaging)

' UML 2 notation: no PlantUML "C" circles, empty compartments hidden
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle
hide empty methods
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 100

' ============================
' Classes (as implemented)
' ============================

class User <<Django>> {
  +id : Integer {id, readOnly}
  +username : String {unique}
  -password : String
  +is_active : Boolean = true
}

class Conversation {
  +id : Integer {id, readOnly}
  +is_group : Boolean = false
  +name : String = ""
  +created_at : DateTime {readOnly}
}

class Message {
  +id : Integer {id, readOnly}
  +content : String
  +created_at : DateTime {readOnly}
}

' ============================
' Associations
' ============================

Conversation "+conversations 0..*" -- "+participants 2..*" User : participates in <
Conversation "+conversation 1" *-- "+messages 0..*" Message : contains >
Message "+messages 0..*" --> "+author 1" User : written by >

' ============================
' Constraints
' ============================

note right of Conversation
  {not is_group implies participants->size() = 2}
  {not is_group implies name = ''}
  {name.size() <= 100}
  {at most one private conversation per pair of users}
  is_group is set by the server, never by the client.
end note

note bottom of Message
  {content <> ''}
  The author is the logged-in user, never sent by the client.
  Deleting a conversation deletes its messages (composition).
end note

note left of User
  Account deletion is a soft delete:
  is_active = false, password unusable,
  the user's messages stay visible.
  password is stored hashed.
end note

@enduml